  "content": "<b>Meaning/Usage</b>: A little; kind of\n<b>Explanation</b>: Usually used to express a lesser degree.\n\"Dinner was <b>sort of</b> expensive.\"\n\"I <b>sort of</b> like her.\"\n\"I <b>sort of</b> know how to cook.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"Do you know how to get to the airport?\"\n<b>B.</b> \"<b>Sort of</b>. But it's hard for me to explain.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"Never mind then, I will just look the directions up.\"\n<b>B.</b> \"Sorry I couldn't be more help.\"\nOther Common Sentences\n\"A little bit.\"\n\"I kind of know.\"",
